About
This repository contains a pure input/output "bedieneinheit" (HMI panel) built with ESPHome
for Home Assistant. It targets an Olimex ESP32-POE-ISO driving one MCP23017 that reads 12
individual pushbuttons (digits 0-9 plus dedicated ARM/DISARM buttons) and drives 4 status
LEDs (Armed/Disarmed/Alarm/Aktiv). All alarm logic - PIN validation, arm/disarm state, door
contacts, entry delay, siren, lockout, users - lives in Home Assistant, not on the device.
Meant to be built into a JUNG LS 990 single-gang cover with a custom laser-cut face plate.

Important Notice
This project was created with the help of Anthropic's Claude (Claude Code).
The code is an experiment to demonstrate what AI-assisted development can build.
No warranty is provided for correctness, safety, or fitness for production use.
Use at your own risk.
